An empty slot describes itself, as CAP_NONE with no rights, rather than failing as every call on it does.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a describing call described a slot that names nothing
Witness: fuzz clock-region-reads-only

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -1248,7 +1248,7 @@ static int dispatch(struct thread *t, uint32_t op, uint32_t slot, uint32_t *arg)
     struct cap cap;
     int err = cap_lookup(table, slot_index(slot), &cap);
     if (err != KERR_OK) {
-        return err;
+        return op == OP_CAP_INFO ? cap_info(&(struct cap){ 0 }, arg) : err;
